flowchart TD
    A[Start: generate_pilot scenario_id, project_root] --> B[Load benchmark defaults]
    B --> C[Resolve n_buyers, world_seed, corruption_seed]

    C --> D[Clean latent world RNG]
    D --> E[Load calibration parameters]
    D --> F[Load scenario config]
    D --> G[Load observation window]

    E --> H[Generate latent buyers]
    F --> H
    G --> H

    H --> I[Generate latent establishments]
    I --> J[Generate latent procurement needs]
    J --> K[Generate latent contract cycles]
    K --> L[Build true_relations]
    L --> M[Generate notice families and clean_notices]
    M --> M1["Assign schema_family_true per notice:
    probabilistic draw by publication year
    (2015-2023 = LEGACY always; 2024+ drawn
    against real by-year EFORMS-adoption share,
    NOT a hard Oct-2023 date cutoff)"]

    M1 --> N{Schema checks}
    N -->|fail| X[Stop: raise validation error]
    N -->|pass| O{Structural validation}
    O -->|fail| X
    O -->|pass| P[Clean world accepted]

    P --> Q[Corruption RNG]
    Q --> R["Assign notice quality class
    (latent HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW, buyer-propensity-weighted)"]
    R --> R1["Two severity-multiplier tracks:
    shared (identifiers/CPV/text/names)
    vs duration-specific (flatter spread)"]
    R1 --> S[Apply dependent corruption]

    S --> S1["Identifiers: missing / invalid / wrong-establishment,
    scaled by shared severity AND a year-regime factor
    (early <=2021 / mid 2022-2023 / late 2024+ --
    a real SIRET-presence regime shift independent
    of schema_family)"]
    S --> S2[Buyer names: variants and generic collisions]
    S --> S3["CPV: missing rate conditioned on
    schema_family x notice_type
    (EFORMS ~ near-zero; LEGACY split by
    APPEL_OFFRE vs ATTRIBUTION), plus
    generic / parent / wrong-related-code"]
    S --> S4["Duration: missing rate conditioned on
    schema_family (LEGACY near-zero,
    EFORMS much higher), plus rounding,
    admin values, unit-conversion failures"]
    S --> S5["Text and lifecycle references: same-cycle
    variation, next-cycle drift, 3-phrase shared
    boilerplate pool, missing links"]

    S1 --> T[observed_notices]
    S2 --> T
    S3 --> T
    S4 --> T
    S5 --> T

    T --> U{Observed schema and no truth leakage}
    U -->|fail| X
    U -->|pass| V[corruption_log]

    P --> W[Write Parquet outputs]
    T --> W
    V --> W
    W --> Y[Write generation_metadata.json]
    Y --> Z[End: synthetic benchmark replication directory]

